-- Tests for uk-interpretation-schedule1.l4.
--
-- THIS FILE IS GENERATED by tools/gen_schedule1.py. The expected values are read from the text by the script, not from the module:
--   * the terms of each entry are the quoted terms at the head of its line (units.py head_terms);
--   * the mark of each entry is the bracket at the end of its line (a year, or a date), and the boundary tests are written from the rule of
--     Schedule 2 para 4(1)(a): the entry reaches an Act passed before the commencement "on or after the date, or after the year";
--   * how an entry defines, what it is in relation to and what it points at are the curated fields of tools/schedule1.tsv, which
--     `tools/gen_schedule1.py check` has verified to be verbatim slices of the text.
-- A failing assertion is a finding.

-- The fixtures: an Act passed on a given day.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An enactment`
`an Act passed on` d MEANS `An enactment` WITH
    `its kind`                             IS `an Act`
    `the day it was passed or made`        IS d
    `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An enactment`
`subordinate legislation made on` d MEANS `An enactment` WITH
    `its kind`                             IS `subordinate legislation`
    `the day it was passed or made`        IS d
    `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`

