§ `Section 5, Schedule 2 para 4 and Schedule 2 Part II together`

-- An Act passed on or after the commencement takes the whole of Schedule 1 (s 22(1)), whatever the bracket.
#ASSERT `section 5 construes the word in the enactment according to Schedule 1` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1979 1 1)) `Person` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS (JUST (`Schedule 1 — the definition of` `Person`))
#ASSERT `section 5 construes the word in the enactment according to Schedule 1` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `Associated state` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS (JUST (`Schedule 1 — the definition of` `Associated state`))
-- An Act passed before it takes an entry according to its bracket: "Person" [1889].
#ASSERT `section 5 construes the word in the enactment according to Schedule 1` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1890 5 1)) `Person` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS (JUST (`Schedule 1 — the definition of` `Person`))
#ASSERT `section 5 construes the word in the enactment according to Schedule 1` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1889 5 1)) `Person` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- An entry without a bracket reaches an Act passed at any time.
#ASSERT `section 5 construes the word in the enactment according to Schedule 1` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 1700 5 1)) `Secretary of State` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS (JUST (`Schedule 1 — the definition of` `Secretary of State`))
-- The contrary intention displaces the section: the text does not then say what the word means.
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 5 construes the word in the enactment according to Schedule 1` (`an Act passed on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `Person` TRUE NOTHING BECAUSE "section 5 construes the word according to Schedule 1 unless a contrary intention appears, and one appears"
-- Subordinate legislation made after the commencement takes the whole Schedule (s 23(1)).
#ASSERT `the entry reaches the enactment` (`subordinate legislation made on` (YMD 1980 6 1)) `Person` NOTHING
-- Subordinate legislation made before it takes only what Schedule 2 Part II names (paras 6 to 8).
#ASSERT `the entry reaches the enactment` (`subordinate legislation made on` (YMD 1950 6 1)) `Wales` NOTHING
